{"type":"text","timestamp":1794861093474,"sessionID":"ses_e19f24ec0ffeI7XnpKUOUNrjw0","part":{"id":"prt_1e60ecb0e001rmXSswK3kedTrJ","messageID":"msg_1e60ec7a2001xVGpN3b9p7Xujv","sessionID":"ses_e19f24ec0ffeI7XnpKUOUNrjw0","type":"text","text":"Refactored `orders/summary.py` into 10 focused functions (all ≤ 21 lines), with `summarize()` as the unchanged public entry point.\n\n**New structure** (`orders/summary.py`):\n- `_Report` dataclass (stdlib) — accumulator for revenue, customers, status counts, SKU units, problems\n- `_discount_for` / `_shipping_for` / `_order_total` — coupon, shipping and total computation\n- `_tally_items` — item validation, subtotal, SKU unit tally\n- `_add_customer_total` — per-customer orders/spent\n- `_process_order` — per-order flow (incl. the strict-skip rule)\n- `_top_sku` / `_best_customer` — final selections\n\n**Behaviour preserved exactly** (verified, not assumed):\n- `python -m unittest discover -s tests` → 3 tests OK, tests untouched\n- Differential harness compared old vs new on **20,020 cases** (edge cases + seeded random orders: missing/None fields, bad qty/price, strict orders, all coupons incl. `TEN` under/over 100, cancelled orders, tie-breaking, non-string SKUs): **0 mismatches**, checked with exact float-bit comparison, dict key order, and problem ordering\n\nOne nuance preserved deliberately: SKU units are tallied *before* the strict-skip check, so a skipped strict order still contributes SKU units, while contributing no revenue/customer totals.","time":{"start":1794861091598,"end":1794861093472}}}
